  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "CiyyfEOmU1WfZK1dxDFdr2c0Ki8=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:39:36.327Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`executeBatch` takes a set of jobs with declared dependencies and lets the reactor work out the schedule. Each job is `{ key, documentId, actions, dependsOn }`, where `dependsOn` names other jobs by `key`:\n\n```ts\nawait reactor.executeBatch({\n  jobs: [\n    { key: \"budget\",  documentId: budgetId,  actions: [initBudget],  dependsOn: [] },\n    { key: \"scope\",   documentId: scopeId,   actions: [initScope],   dependsOn: [] },\n    { key: \"project\", documentId: projectId, actions: [initProject], dependsOn: [\"budget\", \"scope\"] },\n    { key: \"drive\",   documentId: driveId,   actions: [addFiles],    dependsOn: [\"project\"] },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n`budget` and `scope` run in parallel; `project` waits for both; `drive` waits for `project`. One call, one result. The reactor handles ordering, parallelism, and failure propagation.\n\nThe `batch-progress` recipe frames it against the alternative \u2014 four sequential `await`s with manual error handling, no atomicity, and, in the recipe's own comment, \"hope nothing interleaves\". The value is not saving keystrokes; it is that the dependency graph is *declared* rather than encoded in statement order, so the reactor can parallelise independent work and propagate a failure to exactly the dependents that needed it.\n\nObservability comes from the EventBus rather than the return value. The recipe subscribes to `JOB_PENDING`, `JOB_RUNNING`, `JOB_WRITE_READY`, `JOB_READ_READY` and `JOB_FAILED` to drive a live multi-bar progress display \u2014 which is the right shape for a batch, since the per-job statuses arrive at different times and a single awaited promise flattens that away.\n\nNote this is on `IReactor`, the low-level fire-and-forget interface, not on the Promise-based `IReactorClient` wrapper. The recipe's demo runs it against an embedded in-memory reactor (PGlite, no external DB).\n\nProvenance: academy `05-Lookup/00-Cookbook.md`, Batch Progress recipe, academy 6.2.2-dev.45.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:39:35.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:39:36.327Z"
    }
  },
